<title>AUSTRALIA: Australia's SFE wheat futures firm in thin trade.</title>
<headline>Australia's SFE wheat futures firm in thin trade.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The one wheat futures contract traded on the Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) rose on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The January 1998 contract rose A$1.50 to A$195.00 a tonne on a slim volume of eight lots</p>
<p>One trader said the January contract is still being well bid by end users concerned about the drought in Victoria and South Australia.</p>
<p>Settlement prices in untraded contracts were mixed.</p>
